.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "csmp::ODE_StiffSolver::ODE_StiffSolver (const std::vector< \fBSumOfProductsWithExponents\fP > & equations)\fR [explicit]\fP"
Builds the ODE solver, initializing the Kaps-Rentrop parameters for the adaptive stepsize algorithm and a number of other constants used by the solver\&. GROW and SHRNK define by how much the stepsize can increase or decrease in one step, and TINY defines a threshold value below which entries in the solution matrix will be zeroed\&. Memory is allocated for the solution and jacobian matrices and vectors which store temporary variables\&. The system of equations is build\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIequations\fP A vector of ordinary differential equations which define system to be integrated by the solver\&. The equations are stored as STL maps inside of the '\fBSumOfProductsWithExponents\fP' class objects\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The constructor calls the private method AllocateSolverMemory() to allocate the matrices and vectors\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Standard constructor for the ODE solver\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void csmp::ODE_StiffSolver::AssignIndependentProductTerms (std::vector< std::pair< int32_t, std::string > > & ind, std::vector< double > & vals)"
The method uses position integers and new values to change independent product terms in a system of differential equations which was already defined earlier\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIind\fP An STL vector of integer - string pairs defines the name of the independent variables/coefficient, its position index in the equation and its numerical value\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method first calls \fBResetIndependentProductTerms()\fP and then re-assigns new values using STL vector assignment\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To change independent variables in equations without redefining the system of equations\&. This may apply for instance if PT-dependent equilibrium constants are used in a model in which the temperature varies\&. 
.SS "void csmp::ODE_StiffSolver::EvaluateIndependentProductTerms (const double dependent_vals[], std::vector< double > & indep_vals)"
A change of the coefficients in the system of equations, for instance by \fBResetIndependentProductTerms()\fP necessitates a reavaluation of the product terms as done in derivs()\&. \fBEvaluateIndependentProductTerms()\fP was written for this purpose and is called inside odeint()\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The methods requires the values of the dependent variables as first argument\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvals\fP the new derivatives (righthand sides of the ODEs) are returned into the STL vector which is supplied as second argument\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The righthand side values are calculated using the Sum() method of the \fBSumOfProducts\fP class object\&. The terms are added in the output vector at the locations 1\&.\&.\&.n\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The method is called inside of odeint(), after \fBResetIndependentProductTerms()\fP, if and only if independent parameters were modified between solution steps\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
Currently, the method reports the calculated values for each product term\&. 
.SS "void csmp::ODE_StiffSolver::InitialConditions (const std::vector< double > & init)"
Sets the initial values of the dependent variables for the starting step of the calculation\&. In the case of a chemical rate-dependent speciation calculation with the ODE solver, initial conditions are the starting activities of the aqueous species and minerals\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinit\fP A constant reference to an STL vector with the initial dependent variable values\&. 
.RE
.PP

